7445b98 fix(sm): queue correctness — guest fail park, park outlives its sha, pending lost-run (#633) (#634)
===
148:          "id": "revalidate-armed"
151:          "description": "Dead-zone fix (live: fa pr-922, 2026-09-26 — frozen in ai_validating for hours, ticks processed 0): the armed head's dispatched CI run was LOST (racing dispatch canceled by concurrency, or the gh workflow run CLI call failed silently — dispatchCiWorkflow cannot throw). Every existing check is green, but the required CI check is ABSENT from the head, so the rollup reads 'green' while REST mergeState stays BLOCKED. No rule matched: revalidate-armed wants checks=none, merge-validated wants CLEAN, fail-validation wants red, unarm-stale wants BEHIND. 'green' + not-CLEAN here means the arm is stale and the CI verdict is missing — re-dispatch (validate_pr's duplicate-dispatch guard skips if a run is already landing; the skipIfGreenCi flag stops the loop when a completed green CI run already covers the head and the blocker is some other workflow's required check). Armed+green+CLEAN must NOT match — that is merge-validated's merge — hence CLEAN is excluded. MUTEX with mutexExcludeSelf (multi-arm leak fix, live: fa 2026-09-26 — 7 approved PRs armed at once): same self-block reason as revalidate-armed made this rule ship mutex-less, and the same false singleton assumption let it feed the +1-arm-per-tick leak. The exclude-self mutex defers the candidate only while ANOTHER approved PR holds ai_validating; with the invariant restored this rule fires exactly on the one armed approved PR and never arms a second.",
